#{[17592186148124 :question/worked-solution "A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're given $Q(x,y)=4{y}^{3}.$ \n\nFirst, let's differentiate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4{y}^{3})=0\n$$\n\nNow, let's apply $\\frac{∂}{∂y}$ to each of the given options:\n\n- First, we check $P(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+8.$ This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}(x)+8) &=0=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\hspace{1em}{\\color{green}✓}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+8$ gives an exact equation.\n\n- Next, we check $P(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)-2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)-2)=0=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)-2$ gives an exact equation.\n\n- Finally, we check $P(x,y)=2x+7:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x+7) &=0=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\hspace{1em}{\\color{green}✓}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=2x+7$ gives an exact equation."] [17592186171015 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186171019] [17592186171225 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186171226] [17592186171471 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186171473] [17592186172565 :question/worked-solution "Substitute each marked point into $y′=2-xy$. The slopes at $(-1,2)$, $(1,3)$, and $(0,-2)$ are respectively $4,-1,2$. Select the diagram with a steep positive segment on the left, a negative segment at $(1,3)$, and a positive segment at $(0,-2)$."] [17592186172600 :question/worked-solution "Substitute each marked point into $y′=x^2-2y$. The slopes at $(1,2)$, $(-1,-1)$, and $(2,-2)$ are respectively $-3,3,8$. Select the diagram with those signed segment slopes."] [17592186172641 :question/worked-solution "Compare segments across each horizontal row. In the selected diagram every segment in a row has the same slope, so the slope depends only on $y$. It therefore cannot represent the stated dependence on both $x$ and $y$."] [17592186174388 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186174390] [17592186175414 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186175416] [17592186175420 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186175424] [17592186176355 :question/worked-solution "Cosine has period $2\\pi$ and is even. Therefore $\\cos(-x+16\\pi)=\\cos(-x)=\\cos x=-11/24$."] [17592186176546 :question/worked-solution "Cosine has period $2\\pi$, so $\\cos(x-6\\pi)=\\cos x$. Hence $4\\cos(x-6\\pi)-1=4(\\sqrt3/2)-1=2\\sqrt3-1$."] [17592186176547 :question/worked-solution "The shift $10\\pi$ is five full periods, so $\\cos(x+10\\pi)=\\cos x=-1/\\sqrt3$."] [17592186177219 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186177220] [17592186177225 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186177228] [17592186177231 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186177233] [17592186178143 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186178145] [17592186178149 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186178153] [17592186178563 :answer-field/choices #edb/ref 17592186725815] [17592186178563 :answer-field/type #edb/ref 17592186045492] [17592186178563 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186725815] [17592186178563 :answer-field/id #uuid "6e1e465c-e525-5665-8b77-e73f57338bdf"] [17592186179925 :question/worked-solution "At one half-life $H$, $e^{-0.53319H}=1/2$. Thus $H=\\ln2/0.53319=1.3000\\ldots\\,\\mathrm{s}$, which rounds to $1.3\\,\\mathrm{s}$."] [17592186179926 :question/worked-solution "Exponential decay gives $M(t)=M_0\\,2^{-t/H}$. At the stated time, $t/H=1.5$, so $M=100\\,2^{-1.5}=35.3553\\ldots\\,\\mathrm{pg}$, or $35.36\\,\\mathrm{pg}$."] [17592186179927 :question/worked-solution "The remaining fraction is $0.15=2^{-t/717000}$. Taking logarithms gives $t=717000\\ln(1/0.15)/\\ln2=1962404\\ldots$ years, approximately $1$ million $962$ thousand years."]}
